      "source": [
        "## 2. Preparación del Dataset de Rostros Humanos para la DCGAN\nPara entrenar nuestra **DCGAN (*Deep Convolutional GAN*)** sin depender de descargas manuales externas, utilizamos el repositorio público de rostros humanos **LFW (*Labeled Faces in the Wild*)** en color (`color=True`). Aplicamos el preprocesamiento estándar definido por Radford et al. (2015):\n* Redimensionamiento espacial a resolución $64 \\times 64$ píxeles.\n* Conversión a tensores en $[0, 1]$ y normalización simétrica a $[-1, 1]$ con media $\\mu = (0.5, 0.5, 0.5)$ y desviación estándar $\\sigma = (0.5, 0.5, 0.5)$ para coincidir con la activación de salida $\\tanh(\\cdot)$ del Generador."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "cell_data_code"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "lfw = fetch_lfw_people(color=True, resize=0.7, funneled=True, download_if_missing=True)\nraw_images = lfw.images\nif raw_images.max() <= 1.0:\n    raw_images = (raw_images * 255).astype(np.uint8)\nelse:\n    raw_images = raw_images.astype(np.uint8)\n\nprint(f'Total de imágenes de rostros cargadas: {raw_images.shape[0]:,} | Forma original: {raw_images.shape[1:]}')\n\nclass HumanFacesDataset(Dataset):\n    def __init__(self, images_array, image_size=64):\n        self.images = images_array\n        self.transform = T.Compose([\n            T.ToPILImage(),\n            T.Resize((image_size, image_size)),\n            T.RandomHorizontalFlip(p=0.5),\n            T.ToTensor(),\n            T.Normalize([0.5, 0.5, 0.5], [0.5, 0.5, 0.5])\n        ])\n\n    def __len__(self):\n        return len(self.images)\n\n    def __getitem__(self, idx):\n        return self.transform(self.images[idx])\n\nIMAGE_SIZE = 64\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\nfaces_dataset = HumanFacesDataset(raw_images, image_size=IMAGE_SIZE)\nfaces_loader = DataLoader(faces_dataset, batch_size=BATCH_SIZE, shuffle=True, drop_last=True)\n\nreal_batch = next(iter(faces_loader))\nprint(f'Forma del lote (Batch) de entrenamiento: {real_batch.shape} | Rango de valores: [{real_batch.min():.2f}, {real_batch.max():.2f}]')\n\nfig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(8, 4))\ngrid_img = np.transpose(vutils.make_grid(real_batch[:16], nrow=8, padding=2, normalize=True).cpu().numpy(), (1, 2, 0))\nax.imshow(grid_img)\nax.axis('off')\nax.set_title('Muestra de Rostros Humanos Reales Preprocesados (64x64 RGB, Normalizados a [-1, 1])', fontsize=10, fontweight='bold')\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()"
      ]
